//@version=6
// Range Finder [Kalman] v5.15 - Lux Core + Intrabar Wick Trigger + Edge Test
//
// Purpose:
//   Detect a selectable confirmed-HTF range using Lux-style close containment and
//   mean +/- ATR boundaries, keep our trend guards and breakout engine,
//   and warn early on the chart timeframe when price forcefully escapes the range.
//
// v5.15 Edge Test (no detector or signal logic was touched):
//   Hypothesis: after an LTF break signal inside the London window, price reaches
//   Test RR x (distance from entry to box center) BEFORE it crosses back through the
//   box center more often than a random walk would. For a driftless random walk the
//   chance of hitting +RR before -1 is 1 / (1 + RR) (40% at RR 1.5), so that is the
//   number to beat. The table reports the hit rate, a z-score against that null,
//   average R, and how often price reached 1R / 1.5R / 2R / 3R before the center.
//   Trades still open at the end of the trading day are closed at the next open.
//
// v5.12-v5.13 detector architecture:
//   1) Lux-style core: current mean of the range window + confirmed HTF ATR(500).
//      Recent closes are tested against that one current mean and ATR envelope.
//   2) Range Sensitivity mainly changes the envelope width; the default stays very
//      close to LuxAlgo's 1.0 ATR width.
//   3) Our efficiency/slope/drift measures are now secondary trend guards, not six
//      equal votes deciding whether a range exists.
//   4) The Lux band caps the visible range while confirmed price extremes set its
//      actual size, so the SAME box can expand, contract or shift as balance evolves.
//   5) Adaptation tracers are restored and show old boundary -> new boundary moves.
//   6) Rejected-probe absorption is user-selectable again.
//   7) v5.13 replaces the fuzzy LTF distance/sensitivity gate with one visible
//      breakout trigger level: HTF edge +/- a user-set % of HTF range height.
//
// v5.14 LTF changes (no detector logic was touched):
//   A) Intrabar wick trigger. The signal fires the moment the RUNNING high/low
//      reaches the trigger level. Every gate on the intrabar path is monotone
//      non-decreasing within the live bar (high is a running max, low a running
//      min, open is fixed, ATR is locked to the prior bar), so once the arrow
//      prints it cannot vanish before the bar closes. close, body size and
//      close-location are NOT monotone and are excluded from that path entirely.
//   B) Momentum gates normalised against a random-walk null. For driftless BM
//      sampled as OHLC bars, E[N-bar range] = ATR * sqrt(N), so the drive ratio
//      has expectation ~1.0 under the null at ANY lookback. 1.0 is the noise line
//      and the threshold is lookback-invariant.
//   C) Trigger distance floored in ATR units and absolute price units, so a narrow
//      HTF box cannot put the trigger inside the spread + noise band.
//   D) Failed attempts widen that side's trigger (escalation), then reset on a
//      clean escape or a new range.
//   E) Failed-break marks (trigger crossed, LTF bar closed back inside the box)
//      exposed as their own signal stream for the mean-reversion variant.
//   F) Wick and close streams plot separately so they can be compared on one chart.
//
// v5.14.1 plot-budget fix (RE10140):
//   Pine charges TWO plot slots for any plot()/plotshape() whose color argument is
//   a series value, which color.new(inputColor, n) produces. Twelve coloured calls
//   pushed the script to 72 against the hard limit of 64. Dead plots (the two
//   hard-disabled HTF confirm levels and the two hard-disabled probe shapes) were
//   removed and the Data Window set was trimmed from 38 to 26 series. Budget now:
//   2 coloured plots (4) + 6 coloured shapes (12) + 10 alerts (10) + 26 plain
//   plots (26) = 52 of 64, leaving room for a few more diagnostics later.
//
// Containment concept derived from Range Detector [LuxAlgo], (c) LuxAlgo,
// licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. This implementation is rewritten for confirmed MTF
// processing and combined with the existing Kalman/adaptive/breakout logic.
//
// CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
// https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
indicator("Range Finder [Kalman] v5.15 - Lux Core Intrabar Trigger + Edge Test", overlay = true,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 100, max_lines_count = 500, max_bars_back = 750)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inputs
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var string G_MTF   = "Multi-Timeframe"
var string G_CORE  = "Lux-Core Range Detection"
var string G_ADAPT = "Range Adaptability"
var string G_BRK   = "HTF Breakout"
var string G_EARLY = "LTF Early HTF Break"
var string G_MOM   = "LTF Break Momentum"
var string G_TEST  = "Edge Test"
var string G_STY   = "Style"

structureTf = input.timeframe("60", "Structure Timeframe", group = G_MTF,
     tooltip = "The timeframe that creates the range. Example: set 60 for 1H while viewing a 5m chart. Only confirmed structure candles are processed.")
showTfBadge = input.bool(true, "Show MTF Status Badge", group = G_MTF)

rangeSize = input.int(5, "Range Size", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_CORE,
     tooltip = "Approximate confirmed structure bars tested around one current mean: 1~6, 5~20, 10~93.")
rangeSensitivity = input.int(7, "Range Sensitivity", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_CORE,
     tooltip = "Higher widens the Lux-style ATR envelope and relaxes the trend guard. Default 7 is approximately a 1.0 x ATR(500) containment band.")

adaptiveRange = input.bool(true, "Adaptive Range Size", group = G_ADAPT,
     tooltip = "Allows the same active HTF box to expand, contract or shift when a newly confirmed Lux-style balance overlaps the current range.")
showAdaptationTrace = input.bool(true, "Show Adaptation Traces", group = G_ADAPT,
     tooltip = "Draws short old-boundary -> new-boundary connectors whenever the active HTF range changes size or position.")
absorbProbes = input.bool(true, "Absorb Rejected Probes", group = G_BRK,
     tooltip = "If price probes beyond a boundary and rejects back into the range, allow the boundary to absorb that rejected extreme. Turn OFF for stricter fixed edges.")

// Confirmed-HTF breakout behavior is intentionally hard-coded.
int luxAtrLen = 500
float probeAbsorbAtr = 1.00
float adaptiveProbeMaxGrowth = 1.80
float adaptiveMinPriceOverlap = 0.50
float adaptiveMaxCenterShiftAtr = 0.90
float escapePct = 15.0
float escapeCapAtr = 1.50

// ---- LTF Early HTF Break (v5.14 intrabar) -----------------------------------
useEarlyBreak = input.bool(true, "Show Early Break Arrow", group = G_EARLY)
earlyBreakMode = input.string("Wick (intrabar)", "Signal Timing",
     options = ["Wick (intrabar)", "Close (confirmed)", "Both"], group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Wick fires the moment the running high/low reaches the trigger level. It cannot vanish before the bar closes because every gate is monotone within the bar. Close waits for an LTF close beyond the level. Both prints each stream separately so you can compare them on the same chart.")
ltfBreakLevelPct = input.float(5.0, "Trigger Distance (% of HTF Range)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.5, group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Base trigger distance beyond the HTF edge, as a percent of HTF range height.")
ltfBreakMinAtr = input.float(0.35, "Trigger Floor (x LTF ATR14)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Hard floor on the trigger distance in LTF ATR units. Prevents the trigger sitting inside the noise band when the HTF range is narrow. This is the main gold setting.")
ltfBreakMinPoints = input.float(0.0, "Trigger Floor (price units)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Absolute floor in instrument price units. Set to roughly 3x measured round-trip cost, or leave 0 and let the ATR floor dominate.")
escalateAfterFail = input.float(0.50, "Widen Trigger per Failed Attempt", minval = 0.0, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.1, group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Each failed escape on a side pushes that side's trigger further out. 0.5 = +50% per failure, capped at 3 failures. Set 0 to disable.")
cooldownBars = input.int(3, "Re-arm Cooldown (LTF bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 50, group = G_EARLY)
showFadeSignal = input.bool(true, "Mark Failed Breaks (fade setup)", group = G_EARLY,
     tooltip = "Marks bars where the trigger was crossed and the LTF bar then closed back inside the HTF box.")

thrustOpenAtr = input.float(0.55, "Min Excursion from Bar Open (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, group = G_MOM,
     tooltip = "How far price must have travelled from THIS bar's open in the break direction. Monotone within the bar, so it never un-triggers.")
driveLen = input.int(6, "Drive Lookback (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = G_MOM)
driveRatioMin = input.float(1.30, "Min Drive Ratio", minval = 0.5, maxval = 4.0, step = 0.05, group = G_MOM,
     tooltip = "N-bar excursion divided by ATR*sqrt(N). Under a driftless random walk this has expectation ~1.0 at any N, so 1.0 is the noise line and the threshold is lookback-invariant.")
useSessionGate = input.bool(false, "Restrict to Session", group = G_MOM,
     tooltip = "OFF by default. This is a filter, not an entry primitive. Test it as a separate variant after the base trigger has been measured.")
sessionSpec = input.session("0800-1700", "Allowed Session", group = G_MOM)

testOn = input.bool(true, "Show Edge Test", group = G_TEST)
testRR = input.float(1.5, "Test RR (target / distance to center)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.25, group = G_TEST,
     tooltip = "Target = entry + RR x (entry to box center). Stop = box center.")
testSess = input.session("0800-1600", "Signal Window (London time)", group = G_TEST,
     tooltip = "Only signals inside this window are tested. Trades are followed until target, center, or the end of the trading day.")

showBoxes = input.bool(true, "Show HTF Range Boxes", group = G_STY)
boxTransp = input.int(90, "Range Fill Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = G_STY)
rangeColor = input.color(#787B86, "Active Range", group = G_STY)
bullColor = input.color(#26A69A, "Bullish Break", group = G_STY)
bearColor = input.color(#EF5350, "Bearish Break", group = G_STY)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Scale / thresholds
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
float z = float(rangeSize)
float scalePos = (z - 1.0) / 9.0
int winLen = int(math.round(6.0 * math.pow(93.0 / 6.0, scalePos)))
int confirmBars = rangeSensitivity >= 7 ? 1 : rangeSensitivity >= 4 ? 2 : 3
int confirmWindow = math.max(6, int(math.round(winLen * 0.33)))
float s = float(rangeSensitivity)

// LuxAlgo's original default is mean +/- 1.0 ATR. Sensitivity 7 maps to 1.01,
// intentionally staying almost exactly on that default while preserving one knob.
float luxBandMult = math.max(0.82, math.min(1.12, 0.80 + 0.03 * s))
// Stay very close to Lux's count == 0 rule. Only the two highest sensitivities
// allow one close outside the current mean/ATR envelope.
int luxAllowedOutside = rangeSensitivity >= 9 ? 1 : 0

// Our old metrics are now generous trend guards rather than equal range votes.
float maxEfficiency = 0.14 + s * 0.032
float maxSlopeAtr = 0.018 + s * 0.011
float maxDrift = 0.30 + s * 0.035
int minTrendGuards = rangeSensitivity >= 6 ? 2 : 3
float breakBufferAtr = rangeSensitivity >= 9 ? 0.10 : rangeSensitivity >= 6 ? 0.15 : 0.20
float escapeFrac = escapePct / 100.0

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Confirmed selectable-HTF feed
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
float chartTfSeconds = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
float structureTfSeconds = timeframe.in_seconds(structureTf)
bool structureTfValid = not na(chartTfSeconds) and not na(structureTfSeconds) and structureTfSeconds >= chartTfSeconds
if not structureTfValid
    runtime.error("Structure Timeframe must be equal to or higher than the TradingView chart timeframe.")

[sReqO, sReqH, sReqL, sReqC, sReqV, sReqTime, sReqCloseTime, sReqLuxAtr] = request.security(
     syminfo.tickerid, structureTf,
     [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], volume[1], time[1], time_close[1], ta.atr(luxAtrLen)[1]],
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

var int lastProcessedStructTime = na
bool newStructData = not na(sReqTime) and (na(lastProcessedStructTime) or sReqTime != lastProcessedStructTime)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Confirmed HTF storage
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var array<float> sOpenA = array.new_float()
var array<float> sHighA = array.new_float()
var array<float> sLowA = array.new_float()
var array<float> sCloseA = array.new_float()
var array<int> sTimeA = array.new_int()
var array<int> sCloseTimeA = array.new_int()
var array<float> sTrA = array.new_float()
var array<float> sAtrA = array.new_float()
var array<float> sKalmanA = array.new_float()

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Helpers
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
f_clamp01(float x) =>
    math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, x))

f_avg_last(array<float> a, int count) =>
    int n = array.size(a)
    int start = math.max(0, n - count)
    float sum = 0.0
    int used = 0
    if n > 0
        for i = start to n - 1
            float v = array.get(a, i)
            if not na(v)
                sum += v
                used += 1
    used > 0 ? sum / float(used) : na

f_overlap_ratio(float topA, float botA, float topB, float botB) =>
    float inter = math.max(0.0, math.min(topA, topB) - math.max(botA, botB))
    float base = math.max(math.min(topA - botA, topB - botB), syminfo.mintick)
    math.min(1.0, inter / base)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Structure state
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var bool sInRange = false
var float sTop = na
var float sBot = na
var float sSeedW = na
var float sAnchorCenter = na
var int sLeftIdx = na
var int sRightIdx = na
var int sRejects = 0
var int sProbeDir = 0
var int sProbeBars = 0
var float sProbeExt = na
var int sLastBreakIdx = na
var float sBreakLevel = na
var int sCandidateStreak = 0

// Kalman state advances once per confirmed HTF candle.
var float sKLevel = na
var float sKVelocity = 0.0
var float sP00 = 1.0
var float sP01 = 0.0
var float sP10 = 0.0
var float sP11 = 1.0

// Latest diagnostics.
var float sAtrSafe = na
var float sSlowAtr = na
var float sContainment = na
var int sLuxOutsideCount = 0
var float sLuxBandHalfWidth = na
var float sHybridQuality = na
var float sRangeCenter = na
var float sEfficiency = na
var float sSlopeAtr = na
var float sDrift = na
var float sOverlap = na
var float sWidthSlowAtr = na

bool rangeStarted = false
bool rangeAdapted = false
bool brokeUp = false
bool brokeDown = false
bool probeOpened = false
int probeOpenDir = 0
int structureEventCloseTime = na

// Drawings.
var box rBox = na

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Process one newly confirmed HTF candle
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
if newStructData
    lastProcessedStructTime := sReqTime
    array.push(sOpenA, sReqO)
    array.push(sHighA, sReqH)
    array.push(sLowA, sReqL)
    array.push(sCloseA, sReqC)
    array.push(sTimeA, sReqTime)
    array.push(sCloseTimeA, sReqCloseTime)
    int si = array.size(sCloseA) - 1
    structureEventCloseTime := sReqCloseTime

    float o0 = sReqO
    float h0 = sReqH
    float l0 = sReqL
    float c0 = sReqC
    float prevC = si > 0 ? array.get(sCloseA, si - 1) : c0
    float tr0 = math.max(h0 - l0, math.max(math.abs(h0 - prevC), math.abs(l0 - prevC)))
    array.push(sTrA, tr0)

    // Wilder ATR(14) for breakout/probe scaling.
    float atr0 = na
    if array.size(sTrA) >= 14
        float prevAtr = array.size(sAtrA) > 0 ? array.get(sAtrA, array.size(sAtrA) - 1) : na
        atr0 := na(prevAtr) ? f_avg_last(sTrA, 14) : (prevAtr * 13.0 + tr0) / 14.0
    array.push(sAtrA, atr0)
    float atrSafe0 = math.max(nz(atr0, math.max(h0 - l0, syminfo.mintick)), syminfo.mintick)
    sAtrSafe := atrSafe0

    // Exact Lux-style long ATR baseline from the confirmed structure timeframe.
    // This is Wilder ATR(500), matching ta.atr(500) rather than a simple TR mean.
    float slowAtr0 = na(sReqLuxAtr) ? na : math.max(sReqLuxAtr, syminfo.mintick)
    sSlowAtr := slowAtr0

    bool enoughHistory = si >= winLen - 1 and not na(sReqLuxAtr)
    int rollStart = math.max(0, si - winLen + 1)
    float rollingTop0 = -1e20
    float rollingBot0 = 1e20
    float closeSum0 = 0.0
    for k = rollStart to si
        rollingTop0 := math.max(rollingTop0, array.get(sHighA, k))
        rollingBot0 := math.min(rollingBot0, array.get(sLowA, k))
        closeSum0 += array.get(sCloseA, k)
    int rollCount = si - rollStart + 1

    // Same center concept as LuxAlgo's ta.sma(close, length): ONE current mean is
    // used to judge every close in the lookback window.
    float center0 = closeSum0 / math.max(float(rollCount), 1.0)
    float rollingWidth0 = math.max(rollingTop0 - rollingBot0, syminfo.mintick)
    float widthSlowAtr0 = enoughHistory ? rollingWidth0 / slowAtr0 : na
    float containHalf0 = enoughHistory ? slowAtr0 * luxBandMult : na
    float luxTop0 = enoughHistory ? center0 + containHalf0 : na
    float luxBot0 = enoughHistory ? center0 - containHalf0 : na
    float luxWidth0 = enoughHistory ? math.max(luxTop0 - luxBot0, syminfo.mintick) : na
    // Preserve our adaptability: use confirmed real extremes when they are tighter,
    // but cap them at the Lux envelope so one old wick does not define the whole box.
    // Rejected-probe absorption can deliberately extend beyond this cap later.
    float targetTop0 = enoughHistory ? math.min(rollingTop0, luxTop0) : na
    float targetBot0 = enoughHistory ? math.max(rollingBot0, luxBot0) : na
    float targetWidth0 = enoughHistory ? math.max(targetTop0 - targetBot0, syminfo.mintick) : na

    int outsideCount0 = 0
    int containedCount0 = 0
    if enoughHistory
        for k = rollStart to si
            float ck0 = array.get(sCloseA, k)
            bool inside0 = math.abs(ck0 - center0) <= containHalf0
            containedCount0 += inside0 ? 1 : 0
            outsideCount0 += inside0 ? 0 : 1
    float containment0 = enoughHistory ? float(containedCount0) / float(winLen) : 0.0
    bool luxContainmentPass0 = enoughHistory and outsideCount0 <= luxAllowedOutside

    // Path efficiency remains useful as a trend veto.
    float path0 = 0.0
    float overlapSum0 = 0.0
    if enoughHistory
        for k = rollStart + 1 to si
            float ck = array.get(sCloseA, k)
            float cp = array.get(sCloseA, k - 1)
            path0 += math.abs(ck - cp)
            float hk = array.get(sHighA, k)
            float lk = array.get(sLowA, k)
            float hp = array.get(sHighA, k - 1)
            float lp = array.get(sLowA, k - 1)
            float inter = math.max(0.0, math.min(hk, hp) - math.max(lk, lp))
            float base = math.max(math.min(hk - lk, hp - lp), syminfo.mintick)
            overlapSum0 += math.min(1.0, inter / base)
    float oldClose0 = enoughHistory ? array.get(sCloseA, rollStart) : c0
    float efficiency0 = enoughHistory ? math.abs(c0 - oldClose0) / math.max(path0, syminfo.mintick) : 1.0
    float avgOverlap0 = enoughHistory and winLen > 1 ? overlapSum0 / float(winLen - 1) : 0.0

    // OLS slope across the same confirmed HTF window.
    float lrSlope0 = 0.0
    if enoughHistory
        float n = float(winLen)
        float sumX = n * (n - 1.0) * 0.5
        float sumXX = (n - 1.0) * n * (2.0 * n - 1.0) / 6.0
        float sumY = 0.0
        float sumXY = 0.0
        for j = 0 to winLen - 1
            float y = array.get(sCloseA, rollStart + j)
            sumY += y
            sumXY += float(j) * y
        float denom = n * sumXX - sumX * sumX
        lrSlope0 := denom != 0 ? (n * sumXY - sumX * sumY) / denom : 0.0
    float lrSlopeAtr0 = math.abs(lrSlope0) / atrSafe0
    float driftRatio0 = enoughHistory ? math.abs(c0 - oldClose0) / rollingWidth0 : 1.0

    // Existing Kalman level/velocity supplies a second view of directional drift.
    float qLevel0 = math.pow(atrSafe0 * (0.020 + s * 0.002), 2)
    float qVelocity0 = math.pow(atrSafe0 * (0.004 + s * 0.0007), 2)
    float rMeasure0 = math.pow(atrSafe0 * 0.80, 2)
    if na(sKLevel)
        sKLevel := c0
        sKVelocity := 0.0
        sP00 := rMeasure0
        sP01 := 0.0
        sP10 := 0.0
        sP11 := rMeasure0
    else
        float predLevel = sKLevel + sKVelocity
        float pp00 = sP00 + sP01 + sP10 + sP11 + qLevel0
        float pp01 = sP01 + sP11
        float pp10 = sP10 + sP11
        float pp11 = sP11 + qVelocity0
        float innovation = c0 - predLevel
        float innovationVariance = math.max(pp00 + rMeasure0, syminfo.mintick * syminfo.mintick)
        float gainLevel = pp00 / innovationVariance
        float gainVelocity = pp10 / innovationVariance
        sKLevel := predLevel + gainLevel * innovation
        sKVelocity := sKVelocity + gainVelocity * innovation
        sP00 := (1.0 - gainLevel) * pp00
        sP01 := (1.0 - gainLevel) * pp01
        sP10 := pp10 - gainVelocity * pp00
        sP11 := pp11 - gainVelocity * pp01
    array.push(sKalmanA, sKLevel)
    float kalmanSlopeAtr0 = math.abs(sKVelocity) / atrSafe0
    float oldKalman0 = array.size(sKalmanA) > winLen ? array.get(sKalmanA, array.size(sKalmanA) - 1 - winLen) : na
    float kalmanDrift0 = not na(oldKalman0) ? math.abs(sKLevel - oldKalman0) / rollingWidth0 : driftRatio0
    float slopeAtr0 = lrSlopeAtr0 * 0.60 + kalmanSlopeAtr0 * 0.40
    float blendedDrift0 = driftRatio0 * 0.60 + kalmanDrift0 * 0.40

    // Lux containment now decides whether balance exists. Our measurements only
    // veto obvious directional movement. Two of three guards are enough at normal
    // sensitivities, preserving adaptability without reverting to six equal votes.
    bool efficiencyPass0 = efficiency0 <= maxEfficiency
    bool slopePass0 = slopeAtr0 <= maxSlopeAtr
    bool driftPass0 = blendedDrift0 <= maxDrift
    int trendPassCount0 = (efficiencyPass0 ? 1 : 0) + (slopePass0 ? 1 : 0) + (driftPass0 ? 1 : 0)
    bool trendGuardPass0 = trendPassCount0 >= minTrendGuards

    float luxQuality0 = enoughHistory ? f_clamp01(1.0 - float(outsideCount0) / float(winLen)) : 0.0
    float efficiencyQ = f_clamp01(1.0 - efficiency0 / math.max(maxEfficiency, 0.01))
    float slopeQ = f_clamp01(1.0 - slopeAtr0 / math.max(maxSlopeAtr, 0.001))
    float driftQ = f_clamp01(1.0 - blendedDrift0 / math.max(maxDrift, 0.01))
    float trendQuality0 = (efficiencyQ + slopeQ + driftQ) / 3.0
    float hybridQuality0 = 0.70 * luxQuality0 + 0.30 * trendQuality0

    bool hybridCandidate0 = enoughHistory and luxContainmentPass0 and trendGuardPass0
    sCandidateStreak := hybridCandidate0 ? sCandidateStreak + 1 : 0
    bool confirmedCandidate0 = sCandidateStreak >= confirmBars

    // Save diagnostics.
    sContainment := containment0 * 100.0
    sLuxOutsideCount := outsideCount0
    sLuxBandHalfWidth := containHalf0
    sHybridQuality := hybridQuality0 * 100.0
    sRangeCenter := center0
    sEfficiency := efficiency0
    sSlopeAtr := slopeAtr0
    sDrift := blendedDrift0
    sOverlap := avgOverlap0
    sWidthSlowAtr := widthSlowAtr0

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Existing range lifecycle / breakout confirmation.
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    float buf0 = atrSafe0 * breakBufferAtr
    if sInRange
        float traceOldTop0 = sTop
        float traceOldBot0 = sBot
        int rBars0 = si - sLeftIdx + 1
        bool absorbedThisBar0 = false
        bool cAbove0 = c0 > sTop + buf0
        bool cBelow0 = c0 < sBot - buf0

        // Bounded rejected-probe absorption. This expands only; it never shrinks.
        if absorbProbes and c0 < sTop and h0 > sTop and h0 - sTop <= atrSafe0 * probeAbsorbAtr
            float proposedTop = h0
            float proposedW = proposedTop - sBot
            if proposedW <= sSeedW * adaptiveProbeMaxGrowth
                sTop := proposedTop
                absorbedThisBar0 := true
                rangeAdapted := true
        if absorbProbes and c0 > sBot and l0 < sBot and sBot - l0 <= atrSafe0 * probeAbsorbAtr
            float proposedBot = l0
            float proposedW = sTop - proposedBot
            if proposedW <= sSeedW * adaptiveProbeMaxGrowth
                sBot := proposedBot
                absorbedThisBar0 := true
                rangeAdapted := true

        if cAbove0 or cBelow0
            int d = cAbove0 ? 1 : -1
            if sProbeDir == d
                sProbeBars += 1
                sProbeExt := d == 1 ? math.max(sProbeExt, h0) : math.min(sProbeExt, l0)
            else
                sProbeDir := d
                sProbeBars := 1
                sProbeExt := d == 1 ? h0 : l0
                probeOpened := true
                probeOpenDir := d
            float span0 = math.max(sTop - sBot, syminfo.mintick)
            float dist0 = d == 1 ? c0 - sTop : sBot - c0
            bool escapeHit0 = dist0 / span0 >= escapeFrac or (escapeCapAtr > 0 and dist0 / atrSafe0 >= escapeCapAtr)
            bool breakoutReady0 = (sProbeBars >= 2 and escapeHit0) or sProbeBars >= confirmWindow
            if breakoutReady0
                brokeUp := d == 1
                brokeDown := d == -1
                sBreakLevel := d == 1 ? sTop : sBot
                sInRange := false
                sLastBreakIdx := si
                sCandidateStreak := 0
                sProbeDir := 0
                sProbeBars := 0
                sProbeExt := na
        else
            if sProbeDir != 0
                sRejects += 1
                // If the outside attempt fully rejected, optionally absorb its wick.
                if absorbProbes and sProbeDir == 1 and not na(sProbeExt)
                    float proposedTop2 = math.max(sTop, sProbeExt)
                    if proposedTop2 - sBot <= sSeedW * adaptiveProbeMaxGrowth and proposedTop2 > sTop
                        sTop := proposedTop2
                        absorbedThisBar0 := true
                        rangeAdapted := true
                if absorbProbes and sProbeDir == -1 and not na(sProbeExt)
                    float proposedBot2 = math.min(sBot, sProbeExt)
                    if sTop - proposedBot2 <= sSeedW * adaptiveProbeMaxGrowth and proposedBot2 < sBot
                        sBot := proposedBot2
                        absorbedThisBar0 := true
                        rangeAdapted := true
                sProbeDir := 0
                sProbeBars := 0
                sProbeExt := na
            sRightIdx := si

        // Restored adaptive refocus: real confirmed extremes determine the latest
        // box size, but the Lux envelope caps those extremes. This can EXPAND, CONTRACT
        // or SHIFT, while rejected-probe absorption can intentionally extend farther.
        if adaptiveRange and not absorbedThisBar0 and not (brokeUp or brokeDown) and confirmedCandidate0
            float overlap0 = f_overlap_ratio(sTop, sBot, targetTop0, targetBot0)
            float currentCenter0 = (sTop + sBot) * 0.50
            float centerShift0 = math.abs(center0 - currentCenter0) / slowAtr0
            bool sameBalance0 = overlap0 >= adaptiveMinPriceOverlap and centerShift0 <= adaptiveMaxCenterShiftAtr
            bool changed0 = math.abs(targetTop0 - sTop) > syminfo.mintick or math.abs(targetBot0 - sBot) > syminfo.mintick
            if sameBalance0 and changed0
                sTop := targetTop0
                sBot := targetBot0
                sLeftIdx := rollStart
                sRightIdx := si
                sSeedW := targetWidth0
                sAnchorCenter := center0
                sCandidateStreak := 0
                rangeAdapted := true

        // One tracer pair per confirmed HTF update, after all absorption/refocus logic.
        // This captures both expansion and contraction without drawing duplicate lines.
        if rangeAdapted and showAdaptationTrace and sInRange
            int prevCloseTime0 = si > 0 ? array.get(sCloseTimeA, si - 1) : sReqTime
            if sTop != traceOldTop0
                line.new(prevCloseTime0, traceOldTop0, sReqCloseTime, sTop, xloc = xloc.bar_time, extend = extend.none, color = rangeColor, width = 2)
            if sBot != traceOldBot0
                line.new(prevCloseTime0, traceOldBot0, sReqCloseTime, sBot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, extend = extend.none, color = rangeColor, width = 2)

    // Start a new range only after the Lux-core detector has persisted.
    bool cooldownReady0 = na(sLastBreakIdx) or si - sLastBreakIdx > 3
    bool wantSeed0 = not sInRange and not (brokeUp or brokeDown) and confirmedCandidate0 and cooldownReady0
    if wantSeed0
        sInRange := true
        sLeftIdx := rollStart
        sRightIdx := si
        sTop := targetTop0
        sBot := targetBot0
        sSeedW := targetWidth0
        sAnchorCenter := center0
        sRejects := 0
        sProbeDir := 0
        sProbeBars := 0
        sProbeExt := na
        sCandidateStreak := 0
        rangeStarted := true

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTF range drawing on any lower chart timeframe
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
if showBoxes and sInRange and not na(sLeftIdx)
    int leftTime0 = array.get(sTimeA, sLeftIdx)
    int rightTime0 = time_close
    if na(rBox)
        rBox := box.new(leftTime0, sTop, rightTime0, sBot,
             xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, boxTransp),
             border_color = color.new(rangeColor, 15),
             border_width = 1)
    else
        box.set_left(rBox, leftTime0)
        box.set_right(rBox, rightTime0)
        box.set_top(rBox, sTop)
        box.set_bottom(rBox, sBot)

if (brokeUp or brokeDown) and not na(rBox)
    color breakColor0 = brokeUp ? bullColor : bearColor
    box.set_right(rBox, structureEventCloseTime)
    box.set_border_color(rBox, breakColor0)
    box.set_bgcolor(rBox, color.new(breakColor0, 94))
    rBox := na

if not showBoxes and not na(rBox)
    box.delete(rBox)
    rBox := na

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LTF early HTF-break trigger engine (v5.14 - intrabar wick trigger)
//
// Design rule: every quantity that can fire an intrabar signal must be MONOTONE
// non-decreasing within the live bar. high is a running max, low is a running min,
// open is fixed, and ATR is LOCKED to the previous bar so the trigger level and
// the normaliser cannot move mid-bar. Once such a condition turns true it cannot
// turn false before the bar closes, so the arrow cannot vanish. close, body size
// and close-location are NOT monotone and are excluded from the intrabar path.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
float ltfAtrRaw = ta.atr(14)
// Lock ATR to the prior bar. ta.atr(14) on the live bar rises as the bar's true
// range grows, which would make the trigger level and the drive normaliser drift
// mid-bar and reintroduce repainting. Locking removes that entirely.
float ltfAtrLocked = nz(ltfAtrRaw[1], ltfAtrRaw)
float ltfAtrSafe = math.max(ltfAtrLocked, syminfo.mintick)
float htfRangeW = sInRange ? math.max(sTop - sBot, syminfo.mintick) : na

// Monotone intrabar momentum primitives.
float excUp = high - open
float excDn = open - low
float driveLow = ta.lowest(low, driveLen)
float driveHigh = ta.highest(high, driveLen)
// Random-walk normaliser: E[N-bar range] = ATR * sqrt(N) for driftless BM sampled
// as OHLC bars, so a ratio of 1.0 is what pure noise produces at ANY lookback.
float driveNorm = ltfAtrSafe * math.sqrt(float(driveLen))
float driveRatioUp = (high - driveLow) / driveNorm
float driveRatioDn = (driveHigh - low) / driveNorm

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LTF signal state
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int failUp = 0
var int failDn = 0
var bool armWickUp = true
var bool armWickDn = true
var bool armCloseUp = true
var bool armCloseDn = true
var int lastFireUpBar = na
var int lastFireDnBar = na
var bool pendingUp = false
var bool pendingDn = false
var int fireBarWickUp = na
var int fireBarWickDn = na
var int fireBarCloseUp = na
var int fireBarCloseDn = na
var int failedUpBar = na
var int failedDnBar = na

// A brand new HTF range clears all escalation and arming state.
if rangeStarted
    armWickUp := true
    armWickDn := true
    armCloseUp := true
    armCloseDn := true
    failUp := 0
    failDn := 0
    pendingUp := false
    pendingDn := false

// Failed-attempt escalation. Gold in particular runs an edge, fails, then runs it
// again; each failure should cost the next attempt more room, not less.
float escUpMult = 1.0 + escalateAfterFail * float(failUp)
float escDnMult = 1.0 + escalateAfterFail * float(failDn)

// Trigger distance: percent of HTF range, floored by ATR and by an absolute
// price amount. The floor is what keeps the trigger outside spread + noise.
float baseTrigDist = sInRange ? math.max(htfRangeW * ltfBreakLevelPct / 100.0, math.max(ltfBreakMinAtr * ltfAtrSafe, ltfBreakMinPoints)) : na
float ltfBreakDistance = baseTrigDist
float trigDistUp = sInRange ? baseTrigDist * escUpMult : na
float trigDistDn = sInRange ? baseTrigDist * escDnMult : na
float ltfBreakUpLevel = sInRange ? sTop + trigDistUp : na
float ltfBreakDownLevel = sInRange ? sBot - trigDistDn : na

// Penetration measured with wicks, not closes.
float distBeyondUp = sInRange ? math.max(0.0, high - sTop) : 0.0
float distBeyondDown = sInRange ? math.max(0.0, sBot - low) : 0.0
float distPctUp = sInRange and htfRangeW > 0 ? distBeyondUp / htfRangeW * 100.0 : 0.0
float distPctDown = sInRange and htfRangeW > 0 ? distBeyondDown / htfRangeW * 100.0 : 0.0

// No composite force score. Each gate below is an independent AND condition, which
// is what makes the trigger separable in testing; a blended 0-100 score would hide
// which condition actually did the work.

// Session gate must be evaluated unconditionally.
bool sessionActive = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionSpec))
bool sessionOk = not useSessionGate or sessionActive

// Independent AND-gates rather than a composite score.
bool momUp = excUp >= thrustOpenAtr * ltfAtrSafe and driveRatioUp >= driveRatioMin
bool momDn = excDn >= thrustOpenAtr * ltfAtrSafe and driveRatioDn >= driveRatioMin

bool wickCrossUp = sInRange and not na(ltfBreakUpLevel) and high >= ltfBreakUpLevel
bool wickCrossDn = sInRange and not na(ltfBreakDownLevel) and low <= ltfBreakDownLevel
bool closeCrossUp = sInRange and not na(ltfBreakUpLevel) and close >= ltfBreakUpLevel
bool closeCrossDn = sInRange and not na(ltfBreakDownLevel) and close <= ltfBreakDownLevel

bool wantWick = earlyBreakMode == "Wick (intrabar)" or earlyBreakMode == "Both"
bool wantClose = earlyBreakMode == "Close (confirmed)" or earlyBreakMode == "Both"

bool cdUpOk = na(lastFireUpBar) or bar_index - lastFireUpBar >= cooldownBars
bool cdDnOk = na(lastFireDnBar) or bar_index - lastFireDnBar >= cooldownBars

// Raw fires. Latched by bar_index so the signal survives every tick of the live
// bar. Arm flags are mutated ONLY on confirmed bars, so realtime rollback cannot
// produce inconsistent behaviour tick to tick.
bool rawWickUp = useEarlyBreak and wantWick and armWickUp and cdUpOk and sessionOk and wickCrossUp and momUp
bool rawWickDn = useEarlyBreak and wantWick and armWickDn and cdDnOk and sessionOk and wickCrossDn and momDn
bool rawCloseUp = useEarlyBreak and wantClose and barstate.isconfirmed and armCloseUp and cdUpOk and sessionOk and closeCrossUp and momUp and close > open
bool rawCloseDn = useEarlyBreak and wantClose and barstate.isconfirmed and armCloseDn and cdDnOk and sessionOk and closeCrossDn and momDn and close < open

if rawWickUp
    fireBarWickUp := bar_index
if rawWickDn
    fireBarWickDn := bar_index
if rawCloseUp
    fireBarCloseUp := bar_index
if rawCloseDn
    fireBarCloseDn := bar_index

bool earlyUpWick = not na(fireBarWickUp) and fireBarWickUp == bar_index
bool earlyDownWick = not na(fireBarWickDn) and fireBarWickDn == bar_index
bool earlyUpClose = not na(fireBarCloseUp) and fireBarCloseUp == bar_index
bool earlyDownClose = not na(fireBarCloseDn) and fireBarCloseDn == bar_index
bool earlyUpNow = earlyUpWick or earlyUpClose
bool earlyDownNow = earlyDownWick or earlyDownClose

// Confirmed-bar state machine: disarm, resolve the outcome of the attempt, re-arm.
if barstate.isconfirmed and sInRange
    if earlyUpNow
        armWickUp := false
        armCloseUp := false
        lastFireUpBar := bar_index
        pendingUp := true
    if earlyDownNow
        armWickDn := false
        armCloseDn := false
        lastFireDnBar := bar_index
        pendingDn := true

    if pendingUp
        if close < sTop
            failUp := math.min(failUp + 1, 3)
            pendingUp := false
            failedUpBar := bar_index
        else if close >= sTop + trigDistUp
            failUp := 0
            pendingUp := false
    if pendingDn
        if close > sBot
            failDn := math.min(failDn + 1, 3)
            pendingDn := false
            failedDnBar := bar_index
        else if close <= sBot - trigDistDn
            failDn := 0
            pendingDn := false

    if close <= sTop
        armWickUp := true
        armCloseUp := true
    if close >= sBot
        armWickDn := true
        armCloseDn := true

// Failed break = trigger crossed, LTF bar closed back inside the box.
// The fade direction is OPPOSITE the attempted break.
bool fadeUpNow = showFadeSignal and not na(failedUpBar) and failedUpBar == bar_index
bool fadeDownNow = showFadeSignal and not na(failedDnBar) and failedDnBar == bar_index

// Backtest fill reference. In wick mode a resting stop order fills AT the trigger
// level, not at the close, which is the main measurable gain over close confirmation.
float earlyFillPrice = earlyUpWick ? ltfBreakUpLevel : earlyDownWick ? ltfBreakDownLevel : earlyUpClose or earlyDownClose ? close : na

plot(useEarlyBreak ? ltfBreakUpLevel : na, "LTF Break Trigger Up", color = color.new(bullColor, 55), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(useEarlyBreak ? ltfBreakDownLevel : na, "LTF Break Trigger Down", color = color.new(bearColor, 55), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plotshape(earlyUpWick, "Early Break Up (wick)", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar, color = bullColor, size = size.small)
plotshape(earlyDownWick, "Early Break Down (wick)", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = bearColor, size = size.small)
plotshape(earlyUpClose and not earlyUpWick, "Early Break Up (close)", style = shape.arrowup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(bullColor, 25), size = size.small)
plotshape(earlyDownClose and not earlyDownWick, "Early Break Down (close)", style = shape.arrowdown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(bearColor, 25), size = size.small)
plotshape(fadeUpNow, "Failed Break Up (fade short)", style = shape.xcross, location = location.abovebar, color = bearColor, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(fadeDownNow, "Failed Break Down (fade long)", style = shape.xcross, location = location.belowbar, color = bullColor, size = size.tiny)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Edge test (v5.15)
//
// Each London-window signal is followed from its fill price:
//   stop   = box center at the signal (distance entry -> center = 1R)
//   target = entry + Test RR x 1R
//   end    = the next trading day starts (exit at that bar's open)
// On the signal bar itself a wick fill's extreme always comes AFTER the fill, so
// it counts toward the target only when that bar never touched the center.
// Close fills start measuring on the next bar. When a later bar touches both
// target and center, the center (loss) is assumed to come first.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool tInSess = not na(time(timeframe.period, testSess, "Europe/London"))
bool tNewDay = timeframe.change("D")

var int   tDir    = 0
var float tEntry  = na
var float tCenter = na
var float tRisk   = na
var float tBest   = na
var int   tBar    = na
var bool  tHit    = false

var int   tN    = 0
var int   tWin  = 0
var int   tLoss = 0
var float tSumR = 0.0
var int   tR1   = 0
var int   tR15  = 0
var int   tR2   = 0
var int   tR3   = 0

// Follow the open test trade.
if tDir != 0 and bar_index > tBar
    bool stopHit = (tDir == 1 and low <= tCenter) or (tDir == -1 and high >= tCenter)
    bool ended = tNewDay or stopHit
    if not ended
        tBest := tDir == 1 ? math.max(tBest, high) : math.min(tBest, low)
        if tDir * (tBest - tEntry) >= testRR * tRisk
            tHit := true
    if ended
        if tHit
            tWin += 1
            tSumR += testRR
        else if stopHit and not tNewDay
            tLoss += 1
            tSumR -= 1.0
        else
            tSumR += tDir * (open - tEntry) / tRisk
        float mfeR = tDir * (tBest - tEntry) / tRisk
        tR1  += mfeR >= 1.0 ? 1 : 0
        tR15 += mfeR >= 1.5 ? 1 : 0
        tR2  += mfeR >= 2.0 ? 1 : 0
        tR3  += mfeR >= 3.0 ? 1 : 0
        tN   += 1
        tDir := 0

// Open a test trade on a London-window signal.
if testOn and tDir == 0 and (earlyUpNow or earlyDownNow) and tInSess and sInRange and not na(earlyFillPrice)
    tDir    := earlyUpNow ? 1 : -1
    tEntry  := earlyFillPrice
    tCenter := (sTop + sBot) * 0.5
    tRisk   := math.max(math.abs(tEntry - tCenter), syminfo.mintick)
    tBar    := bar_index
    tHit    := false
    bool wickFill = earlyUpWick or earlyDownWick
    bool cleanBar = tDir == 1 ? low > tCenter : high < tCenter
    tBest   := wickFill and cleanBar ? (tDir == 1 ? high : low) : tEntry
    if tDir * (tBest - tEntry) >= testRR * tRisk
        tHit := true

var table testTbl = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 7, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20))
f_tc(int c, int r, string txt, color col) =>
    table.cell(testTbl, c, r, txt, text_color = col, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
f_pct(int k) =>
    tN > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * k / tN, "#") + "%" : "—"

if testOn and barstate.islast
    int   resolved = tWin + tLoss
    float p0       = 1.0 / (1.0 + testRR)
    float pHit     = resolved > 0 ? float(tWin) / resolved : na
    float zScore   = resolved > 0 ? (pHit - p0) / math.sqrt(p0 * (1.0 - p0) / resolved) : na
    float avgR     = tN > 0 ? tSumR / tN : na
    color w        = color.white
    string verdict = na(zScore) ? "" : zScore >= 2.0 ? "  edge" : zScore <= -2.0 ? "  worse than random" : "  not proven"
    color zCol     = na(zScore) ? w : zScore >= 2.0 ? bullColor : zScore <= -2.0 ? bearColor : w
    f_tc(0, 0, "Edge test · RR " + str.tostring(testRR, "#.##"), w)
    f_tc(1, 0, "London signals", w)
    f_tc(0, 1, "Trades", w)
    f_tc(1, 1, str.tostring(tN) + "  (" + str.tostring(tN - resolved) + " ran out of day)", w)
    f_tc(0, 2, "Target before center", w)
    f_tc(1, 2, na(pHit) ? "—" : str.tostring(100.0 * pHit, "#.0") + "%  vs random " + str.tostring(100.0 * p0, "#.0") + "%", w)
    f_tc(0, 3, "z-score", w)
    f_tc(1, 3, na(zScore) ? "—" : str.tostring(zScore, "#.00") + verdict, zCol)
    f_tc(0, 4, "Avg R / trade", w)
    f_tc(1, 4, na(avgR) ? "—" : str.tostring(avgR, "#.00"), na(avgR) ? w : avgR > 0 ? bullColor : bearColor)
    f_tc(0, 5, "Reached before center", w)
    f_tc(1, 5, "1R " + f_pct(tR1) + " · 1.5R " + f_pct(tR15) + " · 2R " + f_pct(tR2) + " · 3R " + f_pct(tR3), w)
    f_tc(0, 6, "Random walk", w)
    f_tc(1, 6, "1R 50% · 1.5R 40% · 2R 33% · 3R 25%", w)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MTF badge
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table tfBadge = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 5)
if barstate.islast
    if showTfBadge
        string stateText = sInRange ? "RANGE" : "SEARCHING"
        table.cell(tfBadge, 0, 0, "Structure " + structureTf + " | Chart " + timeframe.period, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, 35))
        table.cell(tfBadge, 0, 1, stateText + " | Quality " + str.tostring(nz(sHybridQuality, 0.0), "#.0") + "/100", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, 60))
        table.cell(tfBadge, 0, 2, "Lux outside " + str.tostring(sLuxOutsideCount) + " / " + str.tostring(luxAllowedOutside), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, 70))
        table.cell(tfBadge, 0, 3, "Trig " + str.tostring(nz(ltfBreakDistance, 0.0) / ltfAtrSafe, "#.00") + " ATR | fails " + str.tostring(failUp) + "/" + str.tostring(failDn), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, 75))
        table.cell(tfBadge, 0, 4, "Mode " + earlyBreakMode + " | Drive " + str.tostring(math.max(driveRatioUp, driveRatioDn), "#.00"), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(rangeColor, 80))
    else
        for r = 0 to 4
            table.cell(tfBadge, 0, r, "", bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 100))

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Data Window diagnostics
//
// Plot budget: Pine charges 2 slots for any plot/plotshape with a series color,
// so every series below is deliberately colourless (1 slot each). 26 series here
// keeps the script at 52 of the 64 hard limit. Adding a coloured plot costs 2.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Signal streams. Export these three for backtesting; the fill price is the one
// that matters, since a wick signal fills at the trigger level, not at the close.
plot(earlyUpWick ? 1.0 : earlyDownWick ? -1.0 : 0.0, "LTF Wick Signal (+1/-1)", display = display.data_window)
plot(earlyUpClose ? 1.0 : earlyDownClose ? -1.0 : 0.0, "LTF Close Signal (+1/-1)", display = display.data_window)
plot(fadeUpNow ? -1.0 : fadeDownNow ? 1.0 : 0.0, "Failed Break Fade (+1/-1)", display = display.data_window)
plot(earlyFillPrice, "LTF Signal Fill Price", display = display.data_window)
plot(brokeUp ? 1.0 : brokeDown ? -1.0 : 0.0, "HTF Confirmed Break (+1/-1)", display = display.data_window)

// HTF range geometry and detector state.
plot(sInRange ? sTop : na, "HTF Range Top", display = display.data_window)
plot(sInRange ? sBot : na, "HTF Range Bottom", display = display.data_window)
plot(sRangeCenter, "HTF Range Mean", display = display.data_window)
plot(sHybridQuality, "HTF Lux-Core Range Quality (0-100)", display = display.data_window)
plot(float(sLuxOutsideCount), "HTF Lux Outside-Close Count", display = display.data_window)
plot(sContainment, "HTF Close Containment (%)", display = display.data_window)
plot(sEfficiency, "HTF Path Efficiency", display = display.data_window)
plot(sSlopeAtr, "HTF Slope / ATR", display = display.data_window)
plot(sDrift, "HTF Drift Ratio", display = display.data_window)
plot(sWidthSlowAtr, "HTF Range Width / Slow ATR", display = display.data_window)
plot(sSlowAtr, "HTF Slow ATR Baseline", display = display.data_window)

// LTF trigger geometry. Escalated distances already include the failure multiplier,
// so the base distance is recoverable as escalated / (1 + escalate * fails).
plot(trigDistUp, "LTF Trigger Distance Up (escalated)", display = display.data_window)
plot(trigDistDn, "LTF Trigger Distance Down (escalated)", display = display.data_window)
plot(float(failUp), "Failed Up Attempts", display = display.data_window)
plot(float(failDn), "Failed Down Attempts", display = display.data_window)
plot(distPctUp, "LTF Bull Distance Beyond Range (%)", display = display.data_window)
plot(distPctDown, "LTF Bear Distance Beyond Range (%)", display = display.data_window)

// Momentum primitives. Drive ratio is normalised so 1.0 is the random-walk
// expectation at any lookback; log these to calibrate driveRatioMin on real data.
plot(driveRatioUp, "LTF Drive Ratio Up (noise=1.0)", display = display.data_window)
plot(driveRatioDn, "LTF Drive Ratio Down (noise=1.0)", display = display.data_window)
plot(excUp / ltfAtrSafe, "LTF Excursion From Open Up (ATR)", display = display.data_window)
plot(excDn / ltfAtrSafe, "LTF Excursion From Open Down (ATR)", display = display.data_window)

